Itinera split licensing
=======================

Copyright (c) 2026 Patrick Leiverkus

Itinera is distributed under a split licence:

- itinera-core: the reusable, GUI-free numerical library in `core/`, and the
  Python package built from it, are licensed under the MIT License.
- itinera-plugin: the QGIS plugin integration and packaging code, including
  `__init__.py`, `plugin.py`, `provider.py`, `algorithms/`, `gui/`,
  `metadata.txt`, and plugin packaging scripts, are licensed under the GNU
  General Public License version 3 (GPL-3.0-only).

The MIT-licensed core may be used under the MIT terms when used on its own. The
QGIS plugin distribution as a whole is GPLv3 because it combines the MIT core
with GPL plugin code.

The full GPLv3 text is published by the Free Software Foundation:

https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt


